(5870577, 852843, 69008, '<td valign="top">The camera''s automatic metering system is trying to create a neutral grey (18% luminosity) average brightness overall for the whole scene in the image, which is about what this image shows. Neutral grey is a pretty dark grey.<br/> To get well exposed shots in snow or on the beach, you have to set the camera EV (exposure value) setting to +1 or +2. There may also be a "scene" setting for beach or snow shooting that you can use. Check in your camera manual. <br/>Don''t be afraid to experiment with the camera''s settings. You can always go back to full automatic.</td>', 'The camera''s automatic metering system is trying to create a neutral grey (18% luminosity) average brightness overall for the whole scene in the image, which is about what this image shows. Neutral grey is a pretty dark grey. To get well exposed shots in snow or on the beach, you have to set the camera EV (exposure value) setting to +1 or +2. There may also be a "scene" setting for beach or snow shooting that you can use. Check in your camera manual. Don''t be afraid to experiment with the camera''s settings. You can always go back to full automatic.', '2010-02-17 03:13:58.000000', NULL, 0),
